Chapter: RocClosureCapturesParam
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_regression_repros.zig, B024
 "nested closure captures enclosing lambda parameter" and B052 "stored
 returned closure preserves captured values":

     main = (|x| { g = || x   g() })(1.I64)                       1

     x : U8 = 10
     process = |y| |_| [x, y]
     main = { f = process(1.U8)   f(0.U8) }                        [10, 1]

 The first closure is nullary in Roc and takes an ignored Integer here. The
 second captures a top-level constant and a parameter, is stored, and is
 entered later; the list prints joined.

Section: Functions

  ten : Integer
  ten = 10

  process : Integer -> (Integer -> List Integer)
  process (y) = \ignored -> [ten, y]

  join-ints : List Integer, Integer -> Text
  join-ints (xs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length xs then ""
   else if i + 1 == list-length xs then show (list-at xs i)
   else show (list-at xs i) & ", " & join-ints xs (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show ((\x -> let g = \ignored -> x in g 0) 1))
   let f = process 1
   in print-line-uni ("[" & join-ints (f 0) 0 & "]")
  end
